{
  "inventory": {
    "consumers": [
      "spike-alpha",
      "spike-beta",
      "spike-gamma"
    ],
    "routes": [
      "orders-route",
      "billing-route"
    ]
  },
  "base_manifest": {
    "apisix_version": "3.19.0",
    "window_start": "2026-10-13T10:00:00Z",
    "window_end": "2026-10-13T10:10:00Z",
    "start_settled": true,
    "end_settled": true,
    "no_restart": true,
    "disabled_labels": [],
    "route_coverage": {
      "orders-route": true,
      "billing-route": true
    }
  },
  "note": "series are abstract: one entry per exact series; 'start'/'end' null = absent at that boundary. Expected rows are ordered by (consumer, route). Limitations are the sorted set of codes that apply to the row: window reasons (only when the window is invalid), else route-level (GWM_CONSUMER_LABEL_DISABLED, GWM_ROUTE_COVERAGE_ABSENT, GWM_ROUTE_PROMETHEUS_DISABLED) and route-wide series codes (GWM_SERIES_ONE_BOUNDARY, GWM_COUNTER_DECREASED, GWM_UNATTRIBUTED_UPSTREAM) of the row's Route.",
